{
  "id": "sizing_steam_pipes__lb_h_",
  "title": "Sizing Steam Pipes (lb/h)",
  "description": "Calculate steam pipe capacity based on gauge pressure, pipe size, and steam velocity. This tool is used for sizing steam pipes (Schedule 80) in imperial units (lb/h). The recommended steam velocity is 80 ft/sec. Reference: A 4 inch sch. 80 steel pipe with 100 psi steam pressure has a capacity of 5923 lb/h at 80 ft/s velocity.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Sizing Steam Pipes (lb/h)\n\nSteam is a compressible gas where the capacity of a pipe line depends on the size of the pipe and the steam pressure.\n\n**Recommended steam velocity:** 80 ft/sec\n\nThis calculator uses a lookup table for Schedule 80 steel pipes to determine steam capacity based on:\n- Gauge Pressure (psi): 5, 10, 20, 30, 40, 60, 80, 100, 120, 150, 200\n- Pipe Size (inches): 1/2\", 3/4\", 1\", 1 1/4\", 1 1/2\", 2\", 2 1/2\", 3\", 4\", 5\", 6\", 8\", 10\", 12\"\n- Steam Velocity (ft/s): 50, 80, 120\n\nSelect your steam pressure and pipe size to find the corresponding capacity at different velocities."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "gauge_pressure",
          "label": "Gauge Pressure",
          "type": "select",
          "unit": "psi",
